{
 "why": "feature 449 T166 (ask:449-phase4-slices Q10): each `.py` unit a slice's cut ports and deletes, by its `path::qualname`, mapped to the unit it became (`to`, a Rust item's `path::qualname`) and the task that ported it (`by`, `<feature> <task>`); `make claims-rekey` (which make land runs) carries each of its claims' index rows onto the port, owed a full check of the new code, and the push refuses a claim on a deleted `.py` unit this map does not carry. Under `retired` (feature 449 T184, ask:449-T184-elongated-retired and ask:449-T184-elongated-retired-2), each `.py` unit deleted and not ported because the research overruled its rule, with the task that removed it (`by`), the research page that overrules it (`page`, `research/questions/<file>.html`, a file in the tree), why (`why`, one line) and the claims round's finding against its rule (`finding`, `<path>::<qualname>#<label>`): the push lets its claims go only where the unit is gone and the merge base's row of its `finding` (a key of the same label) reads DRIFTED or MISLABELED (any other verdict is a new ask, `make arbiter-ask`; ask:449-T184-elongated-retired-2), and `make claims-rekey` drops their index rows and deferred entries. Under `rebuilt` (feature 449 T152, ask:449-T152-rebuilt-claims), each `.py` FILE a phase task deleted after rebuilding its job in Rust from a derivation judged SOUND, blind to the old code ('An algorithm is rebuilt, never ported'), with that task (`by`, `<feature> <task>`, whose block names the file on its `old-code:` line, literally or by a glob), the Rust module or directory doing the file's job now (`as`, a path or a list of paths in the tree) and the task's derivation (`derivation`, its block's `derivation:` line, a file in the tree): a unit with its own `ports` or `retired` entry is handled there and `rebuilt` covers the file's other units; the push refuses a rebuilt file still in the tree, and lets its units' claims go only once nothing under `as` is owed (`make claims-owed`), the rebuilt code's own `Research:` lines each checked fresh - no old claim is matched to the new code; `make claims-rekey` drops their index rows and deferred entries Three more outcomes of a port (feature 449 T212, ask:449-T212-stranded-claims), each gated exactly so: (A) an entry marked `\"relabeled\": true` lets a claim its port does not carry word for word go, dropped and not carried, only where the merge base's row of that Python claim reads MISLABELED and a target carries a claim of the same label with a checked row; (B) an entry's `to` may be a list, a split unit's claims each carried to the one target whose unit carries its own text; (C) a claim of NONE research whose unit is gone and whose file a port's cut deleted is dropped only when every other claim of that file is carried or dropped by these rules. Anything else - a Python row not MISLABELED, a claim text on no listed target, a stranded claim citing research - is a new ask.",
